{
  "level": "native cold replay from synthesized four-bit GPS L1 C/A I/Q; separate static ECEF truth",
  "motion": "equator, longitude zero, WGS84 ellipsoid height zero; fixed antenna phase center at ECEF [6378137,0,0] m",
  "waveform": {
    "sample_rate_hz": 16368000,
    "duration_s": 90,
    "prns": [
      1,
      2,
      3,
      4,
      5,
      6,
      7
    ],
    "mask_deg": 5,
    "noise": "seeded complex Gaussian, per-axis standard deviation 0.7",
    "neutral": "common code and carrier delay, zenith delay \u00d7 1.001 / sqrt(0.002001 + sin(elevation)^2)",
    "echo": "one horizontal mirror plane, geometric excess range 2 \u00d7 reflector height \u00d7 sin(elevation). Signed voltage ratio applies to a coherent second copy of the spreading code and data. The excess range and its derivative delay the code and shift carrier phase and Doppler."
  },
  "conditions": "All scenario truth, geometry, and noise draws match within each seed. Start navigation bit, broadcast clocks and message epochs are fixed. Each cold receiver gets only the EIQ sample stream. Lock is first reported on the 200 ms status grid. All valid fixes are included in the error percentiles.",
